quran[20]{c,v,t}:
  15,32,He (Allah) said: ‘O Iblis! What excuse do you have that you are not with those who have prostrated?’
  15,33,"He (Iblis) said: ‘I cannot be the one to prostrate before a human being whom You have created from dried clay, formed from ageing, dark mud.’"
  15,34,He (Allah) said: ‘Get out from here (i.e. Paradise). For surely you are accursed.
  15,35,"And, indeed, the curse shall be upon you till the Day of Judgement.’"
  15,36,He (Iblis) said: ‘My Lord! Grant me respite till the Day they are resurrected.’
  15,37,"He (Allah) said: ‘You are indeed among those granted respite,"
  15,38,till the Day of the known moment.’
  15,39,"He (Iblis) said: ‘My Lord! As You have caused me to go astray, I will surely glamorise (evil) for them on the earth, and I will surely lead them all astray,"
  15,40,except for those among them who are Your exclusively chosen servants.’
  15,41,He (Allah) said: ‘This is a path (leading) straight to Me.
  15,42,Surely you shall have no control over My servants—except those deviators who follow you.
  15,43,"Indeed, Hell shall be the promised place for them all."
  15,44,"It has seven gates; for each gate, there is a separate (allotted) portion of them.’"
  15,45,"Surely, the God-conscious will be in (the middle of) gardens and springs."
  15,46,"(They will be told:) ‘Enter them in peace, being secure.’"
  15,47,"And We shall remove whatever bitterness lies within their breasts; (they shall be sitting) as brothers, upon couches, facing one another."
  15,48,"No tiredness will touch them, nor will they (ever) be expelled from it."
  15,49,"Inform My servants that I am indeed the Most-Forgiving, the All-Merciful,"
  15,50,and that My punishment is indeed the most painful torment.
  15,51,"And inform them about the guests of Ibrahim (Abraham),"
